body:
Returning undefined for empty arrays (columns.length === 0) changes the behavior compared to the original code. Previously, an empty array would be returned as-is, but now it returns undefined, which triggers fallback to schema.fields. While this may be intentional, it represents a subtle behavioral change that should be documented or verified as intentional, especially since it could affect consumers passing explicit empty arrays to hide all columns.
```suggestion
  // Preserve explicit empty arrays: only treat null/undefined as "no columns" to allow
  // callers to intentionally pass [] (e.g., to hide all columns) without triggering
  // fallback behavior.
  if (columns == null) return undefined;
```
